class="cprv1-section__summary">What this setup means for warmth, heat-up speed, and day-to-day comfort in your rooms.</p></header><ul class="cprv1-warning-list" data-testid="cprv1-section-warnings"><li class="cprv1-warning-chip cprv1-warning-chip--attention" data-severity="attention" data-category="comfort"><span class="cprv1-warning-chip__severity">attention</span><span>Some emitters may produce slightly less heat at lower flow temperatures and may need adjustment during commissioning.</span></li><li class="cprv1-warning-chip cprv1-warning-chip--attention" data-severity="attention" data-category="comfort"><span class="cprv1-warning-chip__severity">attention</span><span>Some rooms may take longer to reach full temperature — your engineer can assess radiator sizing during the visit.</span></li></ul><div class="cprv1-card-grid" data-layout="responsive-metric-cards"><article class="cprv1-card cprv1-card--comfort_story" data-testid="cprv1-card-comfort_story"><header class="cprv1-card__header"><div><h3 class="cprv1-card__title">What comfort to expect</h3><p class="cprv1-card__summary">Room temperature start/end: 18.00°C -&gt; 18.12°C.</p></div><span class="cprv1-confidence-badge cprv1-confidence-badge--manufacturer" data-testid="cprv1-confidence-badge" data-variant="manufacturer">Based on manufacturer information</span></header><dl class="cprv1-metrics" data-testid="cprv1-card-metrics"><div class="cprv1-metrics__item"><dt class="cprv1-metrics__label">Room comfort evidence</dt><dd class="cprv1-metrics__value">Room temperature min/max: 18.00°C / 18.12°C.</dd><dd class="cprv1-metrics__confidence"><span class="cprv1-confidence-badge cprv1-confidence-badge--manufacturer" data-testid="cprv1-confidence-badge" data-variant="manufacturer">Based on manufacturer information</span></dd></div><div class="cprv1-metrics__item"><dt class="cprv1-metrics__label">Room comfort evidence</dt><dd class="cprv1-metrics__value">Room approached target: no.</dd><dd class="cprv1-metrics__confidence"><span class="cprv1-confidence-badge cprv1-confidence-badge--manufacturer" data-testid="cprv1-confidence-badge" data-variant="manufacturer">Based on manufacturer information</span></dd></div></dl><ul class="cprv1-warning-list" data-testid="cprv1-card-warnings"><li class="cprv1-warning-chip cprv1-warning-chip--attention" data-severity="attention" data-category="comfort"><span class="cprv1-warning-chip__severity">attention</span><span>Some rooms may take longer to reach full temperature — your engineer can assess radiator sizing during the visit.</span></li></ul><p class="cprv1-card__implication" data-testid="cprv1-card-implication"><strong>What this means for you:</strong> This shows what room comfort and response time are likely to feel like at home.</p><p class="cprv1-card__engineer-note" data-testid="cprv1-card-engineer-note"><strong>To confirm on the visit:</strong> Some rooms may take longer to reach full temperature — your engineer can assess radiator sizing during the visit.</p></article></div></section><section class="cprv1-section" data-testid="cprv1-section-energy_efficiency" aria-labelledby="cprv1-section-heading-energy_efficiency"><header class="cprv1-section__header"><p class="cprv1-section__eyebrow">Section 6</p><h2 id="cprv1-section-heading-energy_efficiency" class="cprv1-section__heading">Energy use and efficiency</h2><p class="cprv1-section__summary">Evidence on how efficiently your system can run based on layout and simulation outputs.</p></header><ul class="cprv1-warning-list" data-testid="cprv1-section-warnings"><li class="cprv1-warning-chip cprv1-warning-chip--info" data-severity="info" data-category="efficiency"><span class="cprv1-warning-chip__severity">info</span><span>Efficiency estimates are based on system layout — actual performance may vary during the first heating season.</span></li></ul><div class="cprv1-card-grid" data-layout="responsive-metric-cards"><article class="cprv1-card cprv1-card--efficiency_story" data-testid="cprv1-card-efficiency_story"><header class="cprv1-card__header"><div><h3 class="cprv1-card__title">How efficiently your system can run</h3><p class="cprv1-card__summary">Heat source fired: 60s–1800s.</p></div><span class="cprv1-confidence-badge cprv1-confidence-badge--manufacturer" data-testid="cprv1-confidence-badge" data-variant="manufacturer">Based on manufacturer information</span></header><dl class="cprv1-metrics" data-testid="cprv1-card-metrics"><div class="cprv1-metrics__item"><dt class="cprv1-metrics__label">Efficiency evidence</dt><dd class="cprv1-metrics__value">Condensing-likely periods: 60s–1800s.</dd><dd class="cprv1-metrics__confidence"><span class="cprv1-confidence-badge cprv1-confidence-badge--manufacturer" data-testid="cprv1-confidence-badge" data-variant="manufacturer">Based on manufacturer information</span></dd></div><div class="cprv1-metrics__item"><dt class="cprv1-metrics__label">Efficiency evidence</dt><dd class="cprv1-metrics__value">Fallback/static-return use: not present.</dd><dd class="cprv1-metrics__confidence"><span class="cprv1-confidence-badge cprv1-confidence-badge--manufacturer" data-testid="cprv1-confidence-badge" data-variant="manufacturer">Based on manufacturer information</span></dd></div></dl><p class="cprv1-card__implication" data-testid="cprv1-card-implication"><strong>What this means for you:</strong> This highlights where steady operation can help reduce energy waste.</p></article></div></section><section class="cprv1-section" data-testid="cprv1-section-confidence_and_assumptions" aria-labelledby="cprv1-section-heading-confidence_and_assumptions"><header class="cprv1-section__header"><p class="cprv1-section__eyebrow">Section 7</p><h2 id="cprv1-section-heading-confidence_and_assumptions" class="cprv1-section__heading">How certain each part is</h2><p class="cprv1-section__summary">We separate what we measured, what we estimated, and what still needs installer confirmation.</p></header><div class="cprv1-card-grid" data-layout="responsive-metr